---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Testimonials preview | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="Real testimonials in the Red 3 opening quote card style."
>
  <style>
    .preview-head {
      padding-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-5);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .preview-head h1 {
      max-width: none;
      font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
    }
    .preview-panel {
      padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .preview-panel .panel-label {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.25em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }
    .preview-panel h2 {
      font-size: 1.7rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
    }

    /* Shared card shell: double border like .rate-card / .contact-card */
    .tcard {
      position: relative;
      border: 1px solid var(--ink);
      background: var(--paper);
      padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-7);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    .tcard::after {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      inset: 3px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      pointer-events: none;
    }
    .tcard .q {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-optical-sizing: auto;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
    }
    .tcard .q em {
      font-style: italic;
    }
    .tcard .a {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-top: auto;
    }
    .tcard .a .name {
      display: block;
      color: var(--ink);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.15em;
    }
    .tcard .a .name a {
      color: inherit;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .tcard .a .name a:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
    }
    .tcard .a .role {
      display: block;
      font-style: italic;
    }
    .tcard .a .role a {
      color: var(--muted);
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .tcard .a .role a:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
    }

    .t-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-5);
    }

    /* Baseline: Red 3 opening quote mark */
    .r3::before {
      content: '“';
      position: absolute;
      top: var(--space-4);
      left: var(--space-6);
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 2.6rem;
      line-height: 1;
      color: var(--accent);
    }
    .r3 {
      padding-top: calc(var(--space-6) + 2.2rem);
    }

    .hover-hint {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    }
  </style>

  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head preview-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Testimonials · real</p>
      <h1>Your testimonial cards.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Four real testimonials in the Red 3 opening-quote style. Names link
        outward to the sources.
      </p>
    </header>
  </section>

  <section class="preview-panel" aria-label="Testimonial cards">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="panel-label">Red 3 · Opening quote mark</p>
      <h2>Why people keep working with me</h2>
      <div class="t-grid">
        <div class="tcard r3">
          <p class="q">
            Saielle helped a new product team choose the right product
            management tool for their needs. She offered her experience
            generously, asked the right questions, and saved them a lot of
            heartache. I can't thank her enough.
          </p>
          <p class="a">
            <span class="name">
              <a href="https://www.goroadmaps.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bruce McCarthy</a>
            </span>
            <span class="role">
              Co-Author, <a href="https://www.goroadmaps.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Product Roadmaps Relaunched</a>
            </span>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard r3">
          <p class="q">
            Saielle has a great talent for listening to problems, quickly
            understanding the situation, and helping others unpack ways to get
            through blockers and to the next phase in decision making.
          </p>
          <p class="a">
            <span class="name">
              <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/thedailyem/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Emily Tate</a>
            </span>
            <span class="role">
              VP of Product, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/thedailyem/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mind the Product</a>
            </span>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard r3">
          <p class="q">
            Saielle has the rare gift of uncovering the "why" in every
            situation. I've observed her doing this effectively with
            stakeholder requests, product prioritization, and driving
            conversations towards desired outcomes for the business and user.
            As someone who develops products, this ability is not only
            valuable, but critically necessary.
          </p>
          <p class="a">
            <span class="name">
              <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/wesgalliher/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wes Galliher, PhD.</a>
            </span>
            <span class="role">
              Director of Product Management, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/wesgalliher/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Weave</a>
            </span>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard r3">
          <p class="q">
            Saielle is a chimera. She's a design leader with a great mind for
            product, but she's also led product teams. Many of us can claim
            expertise in either product or design, but it's the rare person
            that can speak with passion, expertise and curiosity to both.
            Saielle is that rare person.
          </p>
          <p class="a">
            <span class="name">
              <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/randysilver/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Randy Silver</a>
            </span>
            <span class="role">
              Co-Host, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/randysilver/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Product Experience Podcast</a>
            </span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
